<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viriathus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 139 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Viriathus was the leader of the Lusitanians in their war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from about 147 to 139 BCE. A survivor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galba">Servius Sulpicius Galba</a>'s massacre of Lusitanians in 150 BCE, he defeated several Roman armies with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> tactics and in 140 BCE forced a treaty recognising him as a friend of the Roman people. Rome renewed the war, and he was murdered by three of his own envoys, bribed by the consul Quintus Servilius Caepio.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/viriathus.jpg" alt="Viriathus" width="320" height="694" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eduardo Barrón · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viriato.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
